# Deflecting Palm (CR 609.7a): Chandra, Acolyte of Flame's two Elemental tokens wait on a delayed sacrifice at the next end step
# (CR 603.7c). Bot1 Bolts both, so they die and cease to exist (CR 704.5d, 400.7); the waiting ability still names them, so a dead
# token is still a source to choose, named by its name now that no Elemental is in play (the Palm resolves, nothing is prevented).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Chandra, Acolyte of Flame
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Deflecting Palm
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Chandra, Acolyte of Flame.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Acolyte of Flame.Activate(Ability: Elemental)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Elemental Token#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Elemental Token)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot1.Hand.Deflecting Palm.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Deflecting Palm: choose a source of damage
Bot1.Choose(Elemental Token)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Deflecting Palm; Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt; Black Lotus; Black Lotus
Bot1.Life = 20
